## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to implement zero-trust service-to-service authentication in a multi-tenant Azure environment.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust service-to-service authentication using workload identities and OAuth/OIDC tokens
- Kubernetes mTLS via service mesh or sidecar proxies
- Per-tenant Azure Key Vault instances with automated key rotation
- Infrastructure-as-Code policy gates to enforce security baselines (no secrets in configuration, template signing, compliance validation)
- Comprehensive audit trails and User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA) for detecting credential misuse and anomalous access patterns
- Incident response planning with clear rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: gateway token validation
function isTokenValid(token, tenantId) {
  const claims = parseToken(token);
  return claims.tenantId === tenantId && 
         claims.iss === 'https://sts.windows.net/' + tenantId &&
         claims.exp > Date.now() / 1000;
}

function validateRequest(req, tenantId) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token || !isTokenValid(token, tenantId)) {
    return { valid: false, reason: 'Invalid or missing token' };
  }
  return { valid: true, claims: parseToken(token) };
}
```
